d by environment, stigma, access, and policy.", "children": [{"id": "b33f36d5-b389-4c18-92d0-bee429a0b836", "type": "concept", "title": "promotion, early identification, and referral"}, {"id": "c95e03d7-aeab-46c1-8e29-761143e72f58", "type": "concept", "title": "suicide prevention and crisis pathways"}, {"id": "90fba1b5-25f0-4e01-9ef2-9be1dd1b1aed", "type": "concept", "title": "harm reduction, overdose prevention, and recovery"}]}, {"id": "5252a7f3-b8fd-49b6-a394-0fa2a92bbeb0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Injury and violence", "description": "Uses data and the hierarchy of controls to prevent harm.", "children": [{"id": "a674bd07-fb49-40bc-a5b7-27280b411d20", "type": "concept", "title": "falls, traffic, poisoning, and occupational injury"}, {"id": "3c9a7229-ebcd-4ae1-9900-93ae6442836f", "type": "concept", "title": "family and community violence"}, {"id": "a4cd5982-481f-4e7d-88d7-137a4001d963", "type": "concept", "title": "safe systems, environmental design, and policy"}]}]}, {"id": "49e1ee3a-a75d-4956-be61-06404cd46251", "type": "topic", "title": "Environmental, Occupational, Climate, and One Health", "description": "Recognizes exposure, protects workers and communities, and prepares for climate and human-animal-environment threats.", "children": [{"id": "ec89dec4-eeb4-46a0-b273-abbc8fcf5b00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exposure and assessment", "description": "Connects source, route, dose, susceptibility, and effects to nursing assessment.", "children": [{"id": "4b0d22fe-0b1d-4c7a-8788-ceb8ea8c7302", "type": "concept", "title": "air, water, soil, food, housing, and consumer hazards"}, {"id": "ae34a2e5-2cb2-4899-a7c3-c2bb3f3cb852", "type": "concept", "title": "environmental and occupational history"}, {"id": "0c3d7d9d-1c48-49ef-aa26-72f75c32075c", "type": "concept", "title": "risk assessment and precaution"}]}, {"id": "9fae7556-77ee-42f2-803e-0bdd6dda7199", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental justice and healthy places", "description": "Examines how work, housing, infrastructure, and land use distribute risk.", "children": [{"id": "a81e987d-478f-4718-a931-cf23fca70120", "type": "concept", "title": "cumulative burden and fenceline communities"}, {"id": "977e4f1a-2b10-4229-8ffd-6f56890e2e7a", "type": "concept", "title": "built environment, transport, green space, and food access"}, {"id": "372d2045-2616-4916-a2bf-6274c5911b4f", "type": "concept", "title": "worker protections and hierarchy of controls"}]}, {"id": "c473cbd2-0452-409e-8ae6-71bddd0d0cf4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Climate resilience and One Health", "description": "Prepares nurses for climate-sensitive illness and cross-sector prevention.", "children": [{"id": "3b56bb26-ad03-4030-97e7-de02d32387d4", "type": "concept", "title": "heat, smoke, storms, vectors, displacement, and mental health"}, {"id": "ddcf4eba-4d3d-47aa-ba17-c4f7ae862022", "type": "concept", "title": "mitigation, adaptation, and resilience"}, {"id": "a74c42bd-860b-41fe-8196-1eb2ca6a7a98", "type": "concept", "title": "zoonoses, food systems, and planetary health"}]}]}, {"id": "89c02cd2-46dc-4bdc-80b3-9a9afce45026", "type": "topic", "title": "Populations Experiencing Vulnerability and Access Barriers", "description": "Replaces deficit labels with structural analysis and strengths-based nursing for people facing exclusion or instability.", "children": [{"id": "3381ffe8-7651-4f71-8f19-4d525b9cfb0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural vulnerability and access", "description": "Identifies institutional barriers that appear clinically as missed care or elevated risk.", "children": [{"id": "22820927-db7c-4765-855f-4c3c871ab4aa", "type": "concept", "title": "housing, food, income, and transportation"}, {"id": "810696a0-b62b-4a13-97eb-28bcbe040eeb", "type": "concept", "title": "insurance, immigration, language, disability, and digital access"}, {"id": "311765aa-8880-4c4c-b852-2608d474ccaf", "type": "concept", "title": "stigma, criminalization, and mistrust"}]}, {"id": "57968825-6468-416e-9